# Work items domain (opt-in example)

Copy this folder unchanged to `apps/<app>/src/app/domains/work-items/` in a compatible V1 print. Run `npm run build` or `npm start`; no platform registration edit is needed. The example is outside domains initially and makes no API calls until installed and visited.

Requirements: contract major 1, Angular 21, PrimeNG 21, RxJS 7.8, web target and a host with valid Cognito tenant authentication. Exact package ranges and public options are declared in domain.json and domain.config.json. The backend must separately implement a tenant-protected GET at the configured apiPath returning an array of `{ id: string, title: string }`. This example does not create a backend endpoint. Do not put secrets in domain configuration. Environment-specific public option values and additional declared packages must be reconciled with the receiving print before building.

The host requires sign-in and a valid tenant for all domain routes. Add role names to permissions when needed; that also filters navigation. The backend remains authoritative. Route-scoped state clears on session reset and ignores late responses. Domain code imports only the V1 public facade and explicitly declared packages; do not copy host contracts into this folder.

Keep stable selectors, API paths and domain IDs independent of the generated host name. Cross-domain collaboration requires an explicitly versioned shared contract package declared as a requirement, never another domain's implementation. Domain tests travel with the folder and run with `npm test -- --watch=false`.

Use the host's semantic theme tokens for domain UI rather than hard-coded colors: PrimeNG tokens such as `--p-primary-color`, `--p-content-background`, `--p-text-color` and `--p-content-border-color`, plus shared status tokens such as `--color-success`, `--color-warning`, `--color-danger` and their `-bg`/`-border` variants. The platform config owns the Indigo/Slate palette and light/dark mappings; domains should not redefine those values or assume a specific host palette.
